// ============================================================
// ARRANGEMENTS — cross-cutting arrangement choices (meter, harmony,
// dynamic shape, solo entry pattern). Distinct from PRODUCTION_AESTHETICS
// (which is about engineering/mixing) and from TRADITIONS (which is about
// genre/era/cultural lineage). The same song can belong to a tradition,
// be produced in an aesthetic, AND adopt an arrangement — three
// orthogonal axes. Examples:
//   - Animals "House of the Rising Sun" (1964): tradition=british_invasion_rb,
//     aesthetic=(none / live-tracking-band), arrangement=slow_build_minor_ballad_6_8
//   - Wall-of-sound mid-60s girl-group production: tradition=girl_group_pop, aesthetic=wall_of_sound,
//     arrangement=verse_chorus_2_5 (or similar pop-arrangement archetype)
//   - Dylan "In My Time of Dyin'": tradition=greenwich_village_confessional,
//     aesthetic=(documentary-folk), arrangement=verse_lament_through_composed
// ============================================================

